D("preserve",{etymology:E("From Late Latin praeservare ‘guard beforehand’, from prae ‘before’ + servare ‘keep safe’; the verb developed senses of protecting, maintaining, and keeping food, while the noun can name jam or a protected area.","prae-","servare","-e","Etymonline, preserve (https://www.etymonline.com/word/preserve)."),contexts:[C("preserve.s1","飲食","They preserve ripe peaches in jars of syrup so the fruit can be eaten through the winter.","他們把成熟的桃子裝進糖漿罐中保存，讓水果能在冬天食用。","To preserve is to keep something from damage, loss, or decay.","Preserve takes ripe peaches as its object; so explains the purpose.","Sealing fruit in syrup helps keep it from spoiling."),C("preserve.s2","社會","The town voted to preserve the old market’s stone façade while renovating the interior.","小鎮投票決定保留老市場的石砌外牆，同時翻修內部。","To preserve can mean maintain a quality, tradition, or state.","Preserve takes the façade as object; while contrasts preservation with renovation.","The historic exterior is kept intact even as other parts change."),C("preserve.s3","生態","The marsh is a wildlife preserve where migratory birds can nest without disturbance.","這片沼澤是野生動物保護區，候鳥可以在不受干擾的情況下築巢。","A preserve can be a protected area for wildlife or a sweet food made by cooking fruit with sugar.","Preserve is the subject complement after is; where identifies what happens there.","The protected marsh provides habitat and limits disturbance.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The county called the polluted marsh a wildlife preserve even though it allowed unrestricted dumping and hunting throughout the nesting season.","The county called the protected marsh a wildlife preserve because it restricted dumping and hunting during nesting season.","A wildlife preserve is protected for animals; unrestricted destructive activity contradicts that purpose.")],quiz:[Q("preserve.q1","preserve.s1","meaning","To preserve food is to ___.",["keep it from spoiling","throw it away immediately","leave it exposed to insects"],"keep it from spoiling","Preserve means protect from decay or loss.","meaning"),Q("preserve.q2","preserve.s2","context","Which action preserves a local tradition?",["Teaching its songs to the next generation","Banning anyone from learning the songs","Destroying every recording of them"],"Teaching its songs to the next generation","Passing the practice on helps maintain it.","context"),Q("preserve.q3","preserve.s3","meaning","In “The island is a nature preserve,” preserve means ___.",["a protected area for wildlife","a type of cooking pot","a verb meaning to predict"],"a protected area for wildlife","The island is set aside to protect plants or animals.","meaning"),Q("preserve.q4","preserve.s1","word-choice","The family used sugar and heat to ____ the berries for winter.",["preserve","presage","present"],"preserve","Cooking berries with sugar helps keep them from spoiling.","word-choice")]});
D("preserver",{etymology:E("Formed from preserve + -er, naming a person or thing that preserves; the base comes from Late Latin praeservare ‘guard beforehand’.","prae-","servare","-er","Etymonline, preserve (https://www.etymonline.com/word/preserve)."),contexts:[C("preserver.s1","文化","As a careful preserver of the village’s oral stories, Mei recorded elders’ accounts in their original dialect.","梅是村落口述故事的細心保存者，她用原有方言記錄長者的敘述。","A preserver is a person or thing that protects something from loss or decay.","Preserver is the complement after as; of the stories identifies what she protects.","Recording the elders’ speech helps keep the stories from disappearing.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The preserver of the family photographs destroyed every copy so that the images would be lost forever.","The preserver of the family photographs made careful copies so the images would not be lost.","A preserver protects or maintains something; deliberately destroying every copy has the opposite effect.")],quiz:[Q("preserver.q1","preserver.s1","meaning","A preserver of a language tries to ___.",["keep it in use and prevent it from disappearing","stop anyone from speaking it","replace every word with silence"],"keep it in use and prevent it from disappearing","A preserver protects something from loss.","meaning"),Q("preserver.q2","preserver.s1","context","Which person is acting as a preserver of historical records?",["An archivist who protects fragile letters from light and moisture","A visitor who tears pages from the archive","A seller who burns every unsold document"],"An archivist who protects fragile letters from light and moisture","The archivist takes steps to prevent damage and loss.","context"),Q("preserver.q3","preserver.s1","word-choice","The community museum became a ____ of local photographs and letters.",["preserver","preposition","presumption"],"preserver","The museum safeguards the community’s records.","word-choice"),Q("preserver.q4","preserver.s1","word-formation","The suffix -er in preserver points to ___.",["a person or thing that preserves","a past action that has ended","a condition of being present"],"a person or thing that preserves","The agent suffix -er forms a noun from preserve.","word-formation")]});
