D("prevent",{etymology:E("From Old French prevenir and Latin praevenire ‘come before, anticipate’, from prae ‘before’ + venire ‘come’; the verb developed the sense of stopping an event beforehand.","prae-","venire","-ent","Etymonline, prevent (https://www.etymonline.com/word/prevent)."),contexts:[C("prevent.s1","通用","A metal guard around the heater prevents curious children from touching its hot surface.","暖爐周圍的金屬護欄可防止好奇的孩子碰到灼熱表面。","To prevent is to stop something from happening.","Prevents takes children from touching as the blocked action.","The guard keeps the children from making contact with the heater."),C("prevent.s2","通用","A fallen tree prevented us from reaching the cabin before dark.","倒下的樹使我們無法在天黑前抵達小屋。","To prevent someone from doing something is to make the action impossible or stop it.","The pattern is prevent + person + from + gerund.","The tree blocks the route, so the travelers cannot reach the cabin.")],mistakes:[M("grammar","The fence prevented the children to enter the construction site.","The fence prevented the children from entering the construction site.","Use prevent someone from doing something, with a gerund after from.")],quiz:[Q("prevent.q1","prevent.s1","meaning","To prevent an accident is to ___.",["stop it from happening","describe it after it occurs","make it happen sooner"],"stop it from happening","Prevent means act beforehand to stop an event.","meaning"),Q("prevent.q2","prevent.s2","context","What stopped the hikers from continuing?",["A washed-out bridge blocked their path.","The trail remained clear and open.","They had already reached the cabin."],"A washed-out bridge blocked their path.","The bridge prevented them from going farther.","context"),Q("prevent.q3","prevent.s2","grammar","Complete correctly: “The rain prevented us ___ leaving.”",["from","to","for"],"from","The pattern is prevent someone from doing something.","grammar"),Q("prevent.q4","prevent.s1","word-choice","Installing a smoke alarm can ____ deaths in a house fire by warning residents early.",["prevent","prevaricate","pretend"],"prevent","An early warning can stop a fire from causing avoidable deaths.","word-choice")]});
D("preventative",{etymology:E("From prevent + -ative, through French and Latin forms meaning ‘tending to prevent’; the adjective describes a measure taken in advance to stop harm, and the noun can name such a measure.","prae-","venire","-ative","Etymonline, preventative (https://www.etymonline.com/word/preventative)."),contexts:[C("preventative.s1","職場","The factory scheduled preventative maintenance before winter to reduce the chance of a heating failure.","工廠在冬天前安排預防性維護，以降低暖氣故障的機率。","Preventative means intended to prevent a problem rather than respond after it happens.","Preventative modifies maintenance; before winter sets its timing.","The service is performed in advance to avoid equipment failure.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The preventative inspection took place only after the machine had failed and caused an accident.","The preventative inspection took place before the machine failed, helping avoid an accident.","A preventative measure is taken in advance, not only after the harm has already occurred.")],quiz:[Q("preventative.q1","preventative.s1","meaning","Preventative care is intended to ___.",["stop a problem before it occurs","repair only after damage is complete","make a condition worse"],"stop a problem before it occurs","The adjective describes action taken to prevent future harm.","meaning"),Q("preventative.q2","preventative.s1","context","Which is preventative maintenance?",["Replacing a worn belt before it breaks","Replacing a belt after it snaps and damages the engine","Ignoring a warning until the machine stops"],"Replacing a worn belt before it breaks","The repair is done ahead of failure to avoid damage.","context"),Q("preventative.q3","preventative.s1","word-choice","Regular backups are a ____ step against data loss.",["preventative","prevalent","presumptuous"],"preventative","Backups are made before a failure so files can be recovered.","word-choice"),Q("preventative.q4","preventative.s1","meaning","When is a preventative action normally taken?",["Before the problem it aims to stop","Only after the problem has ended","At a time unrelated to the risk"],"Before the problem it aims to stop","Preventative measures are intended to reduce a future risk.","meaning")]});
D("prevention",{etymology:E("From Old French prevention and Latin praeventionem, from praevenire ‘come before, anticipate’; the noun names the act of stopping something before it happens.","prae-","venire","-tion","Etymonline, prevent (https://www.etymonline.com/word/prevent)."),contexts:[C("prevention.s1","健康","Prevention of tooth decay is easier when children brush twice daily and limit sugary drinks.","讓孩子每天刷牙兩次並限制含糖飲料，有助於預防蛀牙。","Prevention is the act of stopping a problem from happening.","Prevention is the subject; of tooth decay identifies the harm being avoided.","The habits reduce the chance of decay before it begins.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The prevention program began only after every avoidable accident had occurred and no risks remained.","The prevention program began before accidents occurred and addressed the risks that could cause them.","Prevention aims to stop a problem in advance, not begin after it is over.")],quiz:[Q("prevention.q1","prevention.s1","meaning","Prevention focuses on ___.",["stopping a problem before it happens","describing a problem after it ends","celebrating a problem"],"stopping a problem before it happens","The noun names action taken to avert an event.","meaning"),Q("prevention.q2","prevention.s1","context","Which action is part of fire prevention?",["Keeping exits clear and checking smoke alarms","Blocking every exit with boxes","Waiting for smoke before buying an alarm"],"Keeping exits clear and checking smoke alarms","These steps reduce risk before a fire causes harm.","context"),Q("prevention.q3","prevention.s1","collocation","Choose the natural phrase: “a campaign for the ____ of disease.”",["prevention","prevalence","pretension"],"prevention","Prevention of disease is a standard phrase.","collocation"),Q("prevention.q4","prevention.s1","meaning","Why may prevention be cheaper than emergency treatment?",["It can stop costly harm before it occurs.","It guarantees that nobody ever gets sick.","It is only performed after an emergency."],"It can stop costly harm before it occurs.","Preventive steps can avert damage that would require expensive treatment.","meaning")]});
D("preventive",{etymology:E("From Late Latin praeventivus, from praevenire ‘come before, anticipate’; the adjective describes action taken ahead of time to avert a problem, and the noun can name such a measure.","prae-","venire","-ive","Etymonline, preventive (https://www.etymonline.com/word/preventive)."),contexts:[C("preventive.s1","健康","The clinic offers preventive care, including vaccinations and regular checks before symptoms appear.","診所提供預防性照護，包括在症狀出現前接種疫苗和定期檢查。","Preventive describes care or a step intended to keep a problem from beginning.","Preventive modifies care; including introduces examples of early action.","The services aim to reduce illness before it develops.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","Preventive treatment begins only after an illness has fully developed and does nothing to reduce future risk.","Preventive treatment is given before or early enough to reduce the risk of illness.","Preventive action is aimed at averting a problem rather than merely responding afterward.")],quiz:[Q("preventive.q1","preventive.s1","meaning","Preventive treatment is intended to ___.",["reduce the chance of a problem before it occurs","make an illness more severe","replace every medical examination"],"reduce the chance of a problem before it occurs","Preventive means acting to avert a possible problem.","meaning"),Q("preventive.q2","preventive.s1","context","Which is preventive care?",["A vaccination given to lower the risk of infection","Emergency surgery after a severe injury","A report written after the patient recovers"],"A vaccination given to lower the risk of infection","The vaccination aims to keep illness from starting.","context"),Q("preventive.q3","preventive.s1","word-choice","The city used ____ measures to keep flooding out of the subway.",["preventive","pretentious","preterm"],"preventive","The measures are designed to avoid flooding before it happens.","word-choice"),Q("preventive.q4","preventive.s1","meaning","What does a preventive measure target?",["a risk that might cause future harm","a past event that cannot be changed","an unrelated preference"],"a risk that might cause future harm","Preventive steps are directed at possible problems ahead.","meaning")]});
D("preview",{etymology:E("A compound of pre- ‘before’ + view; as a noun it is a showing before public release, and as a verb it is to inspect or try something in advance.","pre-","view",null,"Etymonline, preview (https://www.etymonline.com/word/preview)."),contexts:[C("preview.s1","娛樂","The museum invited local teachers to a preview of the new science exhibition before its public opening.","博物館邀請當地教師在科學新展覽正式開放前參加預展。","A preview is a showing or sample before general release or opening.","Preview is the object of invited teachers to; before sets its timing.","The teachers see the exhibition in advance of the public."),C("preview.s2","科技","Preview the document on screen before printing so you can catch a missing page.","列印前先在螢幕上預覽文件，這樣就能發現缺少的頁面。","To preview is to inspect something before using, releasing, or finalizing it.","Preview takes the document as its object; before printing gives the sequence.","The user checks the layout before producing the printed copy.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The editor previewed the film after its public release, so the showing happened before nobody had seen it.","The editor previewed the film before its public release so the team could review it.","A preview happens before general release, not after the public has already seen the work.")],quiz:[Q("preview.q1","preview.s1","meaning","A film preview is shown ___.",["before the film’s general release","only after the film leaves theaters","instead of making the film"],"before the film’s general release","A preview is an advance showing.","meaning"),Q("preview.q2","preview.s2","context","Why preview a document before printing it?",["To check the layout and catch problems in advance","To erase its text automatically","To change the paper into a screen"],"To check the layout and catch problems in advance","The verb means inspect before final use.","context"),Q("preview.q3","preview.s1","word-choice","Reporters attended a ____ of the exhibition before the doors opened to visitors.",["preview","pretense","presumption"],"preview","They saw the exhibition before its public opening.","word-choice"),Q("preview.q4","preview.s2","grammar","Which sentence uses preview as a verb?",["Please preview the slide deck before the meeting.","The preview lasted ten minutes.","A preview was shown to the guests."],"Please preview the slide deck before the meeting.","Here preview is an imperative verb with slide deck as its object.","grammar")]});
D("previous",{etymology:E("From Old French previous and Latin praevius ‘going before’, from prae ‘before’ + via ‘way’; it describes what came earlier in time or order.","prae-","via","-ous","Etymonline, previous (https://www.etymonline.com/word/previous)."),contexts:[C("previous.s1","通用","Her previous apartment was smaller, but it was close enough to walk to work.","她先前的公寓比較小，但離工作地點近到可以步行上班。","Previous means earlier than the present one or the one just mentioned.","Previous modifies apartment; but contrasts its size with its location.","The apartment belongs to an earlier period in her life.") ,C("previous.s2","口語","It may be a bit previous to book the picnic before the weather forecast comes out.","在天氣預報出來前就訂野餐可能有點太早。","Informally, previous can mean premature or too soon.","Previous follows be and is qualified by a bit; to book names the early action.","The booking is being considered before enough information is available.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","They booked a nonrefundable trip before checking the dates, but this was not previous because it was carefully planned afterward.","They booked a nonrefundable trip before checking the dates, so the decision may have been previous—made too soon.","The informal sense means premature; acting before checking key information fits it.")],quiz:[Q("previous.q1","previous.s1","meaning","A previous job is a job someone had ___.",["earlier than the current one","only in the future","at the same time every day"],"earlier than the current one","Previous marks something earlier in time or sequence.","meaning"),Q("previous.q2","previous.s2","context","“That is a bit previous; let’s wait for the test results” means ___.",["the decision is too early","the decision has already been forgotten","the decision is certain and final"],"the decision is too early","This informal sense means premature.","context"),Q("previous.q3","previous.s1","word-choice","The ____ chapter introduced the character who appears again here.",["previous","prevalent","presumptuous"],"previous","The earlier chapter introduced the character first.","word-choice"),Q("previous.q4","previous.s2","meaning","Why might buying tickets before dates are set be called previous?",["It may be too soon to decide.","It must have happened last year.","It is an official title."],"It may be too soon to decide.","In informal use previous can criticize a decision as premature.","meaning")]});
D("previously",{etymology:E("From previous + -ly, with the adverb suffix -ly forming a word for an earlier time; previous is from Latin praevius ‘going before’.","prae-","via","-ly","Etymonline, previous (https://www.etymonline.com/word/previous)."),contexts:[C("previously.s1","通用","The two researchers had previously worked together in Nairobi before joining different universities.","兩位研究人員先前曾在奈洛比共事，之後才加入不同的大學。","Previously means at an earlier time.","Previously modifies had worked and places the work before the later move.","The collaboration occurred before they joined their current universities.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","She had previously submitted the report tomorrow, before the day on which she actually wrote it.","She had previously submitted the report last week, before the day on which she discussed it.","Previously refers to an earlier time, so it cannot describe an event that will happen tomorrow.")],quiz:[Q("previously.q1","previously.s1","meaning","If two people previously lived together, they lived together ___.",["at an earlier time","only in the future","in two places at once"],"at an earlier time","Previously places an event before the present reference point.","meaning"),Q("previously.q2","previously.s1","context","In a biography, “He previously taught in Lima” means ___.",["he taught there before the period now being discussed","he will teach there next year","he has never taught there"],"he taught there before the period now being discussed","The adverb identifies an earlier part of his history.","context"),Q("previously.q3","previously.s1","word-choice","The software update fixed a bug that had been reported ____.",["previously","presumptuously","preterm"],"previously","The report was made earlier than the fix.","word-choice"),Q("previously.q4","previously.s1","grammar","Which word does previously modify in “They had previously met”?",["met","they","had"],"met","Previously is an adverb modifying the earlier meeting.","grammar")]});
D("prey",{etymology:E("From Old French preie ‘prey, booty’, from Latin praeda ‘plunder, booty’; the noun names hunted animals or victims, and the verb developed the sense of hunting or exploiting, commonly with on.",null,"praeda",null,"Etymonline, prey (https://www.etymonline.com/word/prey)."),contexts:[C("prey.s1","生物","At dusk, the owl waited above the field for small rodents that served as its prey.","黃昏時，貓頭鷹在田野上方等待小型齧齒動物，牠們是牠的獵物。","Prey is an animal hunted by another animal for food.","Prey is the complement after as; that clause identifies the role of the rodents.","The rodents may be caught and eaten by the owl."),C("prey.s2","社會","Older residents became prey to a phone scam that promised refunds but stole their bank details.","年長居民成了電話詐騙的受害者，詐騙者承諾退款卻偷取了他們的銀行資料。","Prey can mean a person harmed or tricked by someone exploiting them.","Prey is the complement after became; to identifies who exploited them.","The scam targets and deceives the residents for financial gain."),C("prey.s3","通用","Guilt preyed on him for years after he ignored his friend’s warning.","他忽視朋友的警告後，罪惡感折磨了他多年。","To prey on can mean to exploit someone or to trouble a person persistently.","Preyed on takes him as its object; for years shows duration.","The feeling continues to torment him rather than literally hunting him.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The owl preyed the mice without on, and the guilt preyed him all night.","The owl preyed on the mice, and the guilt preyed on him all night.","The verb prey takes on before its target, whether an animal, a person, or a mind.")],quiz:[Q("prey.q1","prey.s1","meaning","A rabbit hunted by a fox is the fox’s ___.",["prey","predator","president"],"prey","Prey is the animal hunted for food.","meaning"),Q("prey.q2","prey.s2","context","A fraudster’s prey is ___.",["the person the fraudster exploits","the phone used to make a call","the money after it is returned"],"the person the fraudster exploits","Prey can describe a victim targeted by deception or harm.","context"),Q("prey.q3","prey.s3","collocation","Complete the standard phrase: “Anxiety preyed ___ her mind.”",["on","at","to"],"on","Prey on is the required phrasal-verb pattern.","collocation"),Q("prey.q4","prey.s3","meaning","If a memory preys on someone, it ___.",["troubles or torments them repeatedly","feeds them dinner","helps them forget everything immediately"],"troubles or torments them repeatedly","The figurative verb means persistently trouble or exploit.","meaning")]});
