D("price",{etymology:E("From Old French pris ‘price, value, reward’, from Late Latin precium and Latin pretium ‘worth, reward’; the verb later developed from the noun and means set or state a cost.",null,"pretium",null,"Etymonline, price (https://www.etymonline.com/word/price)."),contexts:[C("price.s1","商業","The price of the train ticket rose after the holiday weekend, so we booked early next time.","假日週末過後火車票價上漲，因此我們下次提早訂票。","Price is the amount of money required to buy something.","Price is the subject; of the ticket specifies what costs that amount.","The sentence compares the ticket’s monetary cost over time."),C("price.s2","通用","She won the race, but at the price of a painful injury that ended her season.","她贏了比賽，卻付出痛苦受傷的代價，賽季也因此提前結束。","Price can mean a loss or sacrifice accepted in order to gain something.","At the price of introduces the unwanted consequence of winning.","The cost is a non-monetary sacrifice: her health and season."),C("price.s3","商業","The shop priced each handmade bowl at thirty dollars and displayed the tags beside them.","商店把每個手工碗定價三十美元，並在旁邊展示標籤。","To price is to decide or mark how much something costs.","Priced takes each bowl as object; at thirty dollars gives the amount.","The store assigns a selling price to each item.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The price of the book was the author’s painful loss of sleep, not the forty dollars printed on its tag.","The price of the book was forty dollars; the author’s lost sleep was a separate cost.","Price usually names the monetary amount, while a figurative price is a sacrifice made to obtain an outcome.")],quiz:[Q("price.q1","price.s1","meaning","A shop’s price for a lamp is ___.",["the money a buyer must pay","the lamp’s color","the shop’s opening hour"],"the money a buyer must pay","Price names the monetary cost of the item.","meaning"),Q("price.q2","price.s2","context","“He gained fame at the price of his privacy” means he ___.",["sacrificed privacy in order to gain fame","paid cash for a private room","lost fame because he was private"],"sacrificed privacy in order to gain fame","The figurative price is an unpleasant sacrifice.","context"),Q("price.q3","price.s3","grammar","Which sentence uses price as a verb?",["They priced the used bicycle at fifty dollars.","The price of the bicycle was fair.","The bicycle had a high price."],"They priced the used bicycle at fifty dollars.","Priced is the past-tense verb meaning set the cost.","grammar"),Q("price.q4","price.s3","word-choice","The gallery will ____ the small prints individually before the sale.",["price","preside","prevaricate"],"price","The gallery will assign a cost to each print.","word-choice")]});
D("price list",{etymology:E("A compound of price, from Old French pris and Latin pretium ‘value’, plus list; the phrase names a written or displayed list of goods with their prices.",null,"pretium + list",null,"Etymonline, price and list (https://www.etymonline.com/word/price; https://www.etymonline.com/word/list)."),contexts:[C("price list.s1","商業","The supplier emailed an updated price list so the cafe could compare wholesale costs before ordering.","供應商寄來更新的價目表，讓咖啡館在訂貨前比較批發成本。","A price list is a list showing how much goods or services cost.","Price list is the object of emailed; so gives its purpose.","The cafe uses the listed amounts to compare items before buying.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The price list showed each product’s ingredients but deliberately omitted every amount customers had to pay.","The price list showed each product and the amount customers had to pay.","A price list provides prices; a list without any prices is not a price list.")],quiz:[Q("price list.q1","price list.s1","meaning","A price list tells customers ___.",["how much listed goods or services cost","how old every customer is","which products are made of wood"],"how much listed goods or services cost","The list displays prices alongside items.","meaning"),Q("price list.q2","price list.s1","context","Why check a supplier’s price list before placing an order?",["To compare the costs of available items","To see which employee is on vacation","To learn the supplier’s building color"],"To compare the costs of available items","The document helps buyers see and compare prices.","context"),Q("price list.q3","price list.s1","word-choice","The restaurant posted its new ____ beside the entrance.",["price list","pretence","priesthood"],"price list","The posted document lists menu prices.","word-choice"),Q("price list.q4","price list.s1","meaning","Which item belongs on a price list?",["A product name with its cost","A customer’s private medical record","A poem with no goods or charges"],"A product name with its cost","A price list pairs items or services with amounts charged.","meaning")]});
D("priceless",{etymology:E("From Old French precios ‘costly, valuable’, from Latin pretiosus and pretium ‘worth, price’, later shaped transparently in English by price + -less; its modern sense is so valuable that no price can express it.",null,"pretium","-less","Etymonline, priceless (https://www.etymonline.com/word/price)."),contexts:[C("priceless.s1","文化","The priceless diary survived the fire because a curator had stored it in a sealed metal cabinet.","這本珍貴無價的日記因策展人把它存放在密封金屬櫃中而躲過火災。","Priceless means extremely valuable, beyond an ordinary monetary price.","Priceless modifies diary; because explains how it survived.","Its historical importance makes it too valuable to replace with money.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The archive called the diary priceless because it could be replaced instantly for one cent at any shop.","The archive called the diary priceless because its unique historical record could not be replaced for money.","Priceless describes something extraordinarily valuable, not something easily replaced at a negligible cost.")],quiz:[Q("priceless.q1","priceless.s1","meaning","A priceless artifact is ___.",["so valuable that no ordinary price captures its worth","worth exactly one cent","available free in every shop"],"so valuable that no ordinary price captures its worth","Priceless means extremely valuable, not literally having no worth.","meaning"),Q("priceless.q2","priceless.s1","context","Which item is most likely to be called priceless?",["A unique family letter written by a historical figure","A disposable cup sold for one coin","A common pebble from a parking lot"],"A unique family letter written by a historical figure","Its unique history gives it value beyond a normal market price.","context"),Q("priceless.q3","priceless.s1","word-choice","The rescued photograph was ____ to the family because it was the only image of their great-grandmother.",["priceless","pressing","preterm"],"priceless","Its unique family importance makes it exceptionally valuable.","word-choice"),Q("priceless.q4","priceless.s1","meaning","Does priceless usually mean “worthless”?",["No; it means extremely valuable.","Yes; it means nobody wants it.","Yes; it means already sold."],"No; it means extremely valuable.","Despite -less in its form, priceless means beyond price or very precious.","meaning")]});
D("prick",{etymology:E("From Old English prica ‘point, small mark’ and related Germanic forms; the verb sense developed as to pierce or cause a small sharp pain.",null,"prica","-","Etymonline, prick (https://www.etymonline.com/word/prick)."),contexts:[C("prick.s1","健康","The rose thorn gave my thumb a tiny prick, and a bright drop of blood appeared.","玫瑰刺輕輕扎了我的拇指一下，接著冒出一滴鮮紅的血。","A prick is a small sharp pain, or to prick is to cause that pain by piercing.","Prick is the object of gave; the thorn identifies what caused it.","The sharp thorn punctures the skin and causes a brief, localized pain.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The blunt cotton ball gave his finger a deep prick by pressing softly without piercing or causing any sharp pain.","The rose thorn gave his finger a prick by piercing the skin and causing a sharp pain.","A prick is a sharp, small pain associated with a point piercing or puncturing the skin.")],quiz:[Q("prick.q1","prick.s1","meaning","A prick from a thorn is usually ___.",["a small sharp pain","a long musical note","a large soft blanket"],"a small sharp pain","The noun names a brief, pointed pain.","meaning"),Q("prick.q2","prick.s1","context","What might prick a finger while sewing?",["A sharp needle","A soft pillow","A glass of water"],"A sharp needle","A point can puncture the skin and cause a prick.","context"),Q("prick.q3","prick.s1","word-choice","The cactus spine may ____ your hand if you touch it.",["prick","prevail","preserve"],"prick","The pointed spine can pierce the skin.","word-choice"),Q("prick.q4","prick.s1","meaning","Which object is least likely to cause a prick?",["A smooth rubber ball","A sharp pin","A rose thorn"],"A smooth rubber ball","A prick usually comes from a pointed object that punctures or stings.","meaning")]});
D("prickle",{etymology:E("From Old English pricel/pricle, a diminutive of prica ‘point’; the noun developed for a small sharp point or stinging sensation, with a related verb meaning tingle or prick.",null,"prica","-le","Etymonline, prickle (https://www.etymonline.com/word/prickle)."),contexts:[C("prickle.s1","自然","A prickle from the blackberry bramble caught her sleeve as she reached for the ripe fruit.","她伸手摘熟莓果時，黑莓灌木上的尖刺勾住了袖子。","A prickle can be a small sharp point on a plant or a stinging sensation.","Prickle is the subject of caught; from the bramble identifies its source.","The plant’s small sharp point snags the fabric.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The smooth, thornless stem was covered in prickles that were broad and soft, with no sharp points at all.","The stem was prickly because its surface carried small sharp points.","A prickle is a small sharp point or a stinging sensation, not a broad soft feature.")],quiz:[Q("prickle.q1","prickle.s1","meaning","A plant prickle is ___.",["a small sharp point","a large smooth leaf","a sweet fruit juice"],"a small sharp point","Prickle names a small sharp projection on a plant.","meaning"),Q("prickle.q2","prickle.s1","context","Why might a hiker feel a prickle on an arm after brushing a thorn bush?",["A small spine may have scratched the skin.","The hiker drank cold water.","The path became wider."],"A small spine may have scratched the skin.","A prickle can also be the sharp stinging feeling caused by a point.","context"),Q("prickle.q3","prickle.s1","word-choice","The gardener wore gloves to avoid a ____ from the rose stem.",["prickle","price list","president"],"prickle","The thorny stem may cause a small sharp scratch.","word-choice"),Q("prickle.q4","prickle.s1","meaning","What word describes the sensation of tiny sharp points on the skin?",["a prickle","a presidency","a preview"],"a prickle","Prickle can name a stinging or tingling feeling.","meaning")]});
D("prickly",{etymology:E("From prickle + -y, the adjective suffix meaning ‘having or characterized by’; prickly first describes surfaces with sharp points and extends figuratively to easily offended people or difficult subjects.",null,"prickle","-y","Etymonline, prickly (https://www.etymonline.com/word/prickly)."),contexts:[C("prickly.s1","通用","The prickly hedge made a poor shortcut, and its sharp branches caught the cyclist’s jacket.","這道多刺的樹籬不是好捷徑，尖枝還勾住了騎士的外套。","Prickly means covered with sharp points; it can also describe someone easily offended.","Prickly modifies hedge; and links the result of its sharp branches.","The spines make the hedge physically difficult to pass.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The prickly cactus had a perfectly smooth surface with no spines, while the gardener handled it barehanded.","The prickly cactus was covered in sharp spines, so the gardener used gloves.","Prickly describes a surface with sharp points; a smooth surface is not prickly.")],quiz:[Q("prickly.q1","prickly.s1","meaning","A prickly plant is ___.",["covered with sharp points","completely smooth","made of paper"],"covered with sharp points","The literal adjective means having prickles or spines.","meaning"),Q("prickly.q2","prickly.s1","context","If a colleague is prickly about criticism, the colleague may ___.",["be quick to take offense","be made of cactus spines","be unable to hear speech"],"be quick to take offense","The figurative sense describes someone easily offended.","context"),Q("prickly.q3","prickly.s1","word-choice","The dry ____ bush scratched the gardener’s gloves.",["prickly","priceless","presidential"],"prickly","The bush has sharp points that can scratch.","word-choice"),Q("prickly.q4","prickly.s1","meaning","Which topic might be called prickly in a discussion?",["A sensitive subject likely to offend people","A simple arithmetic fact everyone accepts","A silent room with no people"],"A sensitive subject likely to offend people","Prickly can figuratively describe a difficult or sensitive subject.","meaning")]});
D("pride",{etymology:E("From Old English pryde, from proud; the word developed senses of satisfaction in achievement, excessive self-regard, and self-respect.",null,"proud","-e","Etymonline, pride (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pride)."),contexts:[C("pride.s1","通用","She takes pride in teaching every child to read, and she keeps a record of their progress.","她以教會每個孩子閱讀為傲，並記錄他們的進步。","Pride can be pleasure or satisfaction in an achievement or someone connected with you.","Takes pride in is the standard pattern; in introduces the achievement.","Her satisfaction comes from the children’s learning progress."),C("pride.s2","通用","His pride stopped him from apologizing even after he learned that his words had hurt his friend.","即使知道自己的話傷了朋友，他的自負仍使他不肯道歉。","Pride can mean an excessively high opinion of oneself.","Pride is the subject; from apologizing names the action it prevents.","His self-regard makes him resist admitting fault."),C("pride.s3","心理","The public joke wounded her pride, so she asked the team not to repeat it.","公開的玩笑傷了她的自尊，因此她請團隊不要再說。","Pride can mean the wish to be respected and not humiliated.","Pride is the object of wounded; so introduces her response.","She feels her dignity has been attacked."),C("pride.s4","通用","He prides himself on returning every borrowed tool in better condition than he found it.","他以歸還每件借來的工具時都比借來時更完好為榮。","To pride oneself on something is to feel pleased about a quality or action.","The fixed form is pride oneself on + noun or gerund.","He values his careful treatment of borrowed things.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","She prides herself of keeping the lab organized and returning every tool.","She prides herself on keeping the lab organized and returning every tool.","The reflexive construction is pride oneself on something or doing something.")],quiz:[Q("pride.q1","pride.s1","meaning","If someone takes pride in a careful project, they feel ___.",["pleased and satisfied with it","ashamed that it exists","unable to remember making it"],"pleased and satisfied with it","This positive sense concerns satisfaction in an achievement.","meaning"),Q("pride.q2","pride.s2","context","Which behavior shows excessive pride?",["Refusing to apologize because one thinks one can never be wrong","Thanking a teammate for help","Admitting an error promptly"],"Refusing to apologize because one thinks one can never be wrong","This sense is an inflated opinion of oneself.","context"),Q("pride.q3","pride.s3","meaning","If a cruel remark wounds someone’s pride, it harms their sense of ___.",["dignity and self-respect","physical balance","direction on a map"],"dignity and self-respect","Pride can mean the wish to be respected and not shamed.","meaning"),Q("pride.q4","pride.s4","collocation","Choose the standard phrase: “He prides himself ___ his honesty.”",["on","at","for"],"on","The construction is pride oneself on a quality or action.","collocation")]});
D("priest",{etymology:E("From Old English preost, through Vulgar Latin *prester and Late Latin presbyter, from Greek presbyteros ‘elder’; the English word developed for an authorized religious minister.",null,"presbyteros","-","Etymonline, priest (https://www.etymonline.com/word/priest)."),contexts:[C("priest.s1","宗教","The priest visited the hospital to offer prayers to a patient who had asked for spiritual support.","神父應病人要求前往醫院，為需要心靈支持的病人祈禱。","In some Christian churches, a priest is an official who leads worship and rites.","Priest is the subject of visited; to offer gives the purpose.","The religious official provides worship and spiritual care."),C("priest.s2","宗教","In the ancient temple, a priest performed the seasonal rites and kept the sacred fire burning.","在古代神廟裡，祭司主持季節儀式，並讓聖火持續燃燒。","Priest can more broadly mean a religious official authorized to perform rites or sacrifices.","Priest is the subject; performed and kept describe the ritual responsibilities.","The example uses the general religious sense, not specifically a Christian office.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The priest led worship in the church, so the word can only refer to a person who works in a secular bank.","The priest led worship in the church as a religious official authorized to conduct rites.","Priest names a religious minister or ritual official, not a secular banking occupation.")],quiz:[Q("priest.q1","priest.s1","meaning","In a church that uses the title, a priest is ___.",["a religious official who leads worship and rites","a person who repairs roads","a type of public building"],"a religious official who leads worship and rites","This Christian sense names a minister who conducts services.","meaning"),Q("priest.q2","priest.s2","context","Who is a priest in a broad historical account of a temple?",["A religious official conducting sacrifices or rites","A merchant selling unrelated goods","A soldier guarding a bridge"],"A religious official conducting sacrifices or rites","The word can refer to ritual authorities in religions beyond Christianity.","context"),Q("priest.q3","priest.s1","word-choice","The ____ visited the parishioners and led Sunday worship.",["priest","prickly","price"],"priest","The religious minister leads the service and visits the community.","word-choice"),Q("priest.q4","priest.s2","meaning","What does the older root presbyteros mean?",["elder","merchant","storm"],"elder","The Latin and Greek history traces priest to a word meaning elder.","word-formation")]});
D("priestess",{etymology:E("Formed from priest + -ess, an older English feminine suffix; priest comes through Old English and Vulgar Latin from Greek presbyteros ‘elder’.",null,"presbyteros","-ess","Etymonline, priestess (https://www.etymonline.com/word/priestess)."),contexts:[C("priestess.s1","宗教","The priestess led the dawn offering at the shrine and explained the ritual to the visiting students.","女祭司在黎明時主持神龕前的供奉儀式，並向來訪學生解釋儀式內容。","A priestess is a woman serving as a priest, especially in ancient or polytheistic religions.","Priestess is the subject of led and explained; at the shrine identifies the setting.","She holds a religious role and conducts a rite in the shrine.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The priestess was a male ship captain who performed no ceremony and had no religious role.","The priestess was a woman who conducted a religious rite at the shrine.","Priestess names a female religious officiant, not a ship captain without a ritual role.")],quiz:[Q("priestess.q1","priestess.s1","meaning","A priestess is ___.",["a woman who serves in a priestly religious role","a woman who sells tickets","a person who writes a price list"],"a woman who serves in a priestly religious role","The feminine noun names a woman performing religious duties.","meaning"),Q("priestess.q2","priestess.s1","context","Which sentence uses priestess accurately?",["The priestess conducted the ceremony at the ancient shrine.","The priestess calibrated the phone’s battery.","The priestess listed the cost of every meal."],"The priestess conducted the ceremony at the ancient shrine.","Conducting a ritual is a priestly religious duty.","context"),Q("priestess.q3","priestess.s1","word-formation","What does the suffix -ess traditionally mark in priestess?",["a female person in the role","a place under a church","a past-tense action"],"a female person in the role","The suffix forms a feminine counterpart to priest.","word-formation"),Q("priestess.q4","priestess.s1","word-choice","In the story, the ____ interpreted the temple’s sacred signs.",["priestess","presidency","prevalence"],"priestess","A female religious officiant may interpret signs in a ritual setting.","word-choice")]});
D("priesthood",{etymology:E("From Old English preosthad, formed from preost ‘priest’ + -had/-hood ‘state, condition, rank’; it names the office or work of a priest and priests as a group.",null,"preost","-hood","Etymonline, priesthood (https://www.etymonline.com/word/priesthood)."),contexts:[C("priesthood.s1","宗教","After years of study, Daniel entered the priesthood and began serving a rural parish.","多年研讀後，丹尼爾接受神職，開始服務鄉間教區。","Priesthood is the work, office, or collective body of priests.","Entered the priesthood is a fixed phrase for taking up the vocation.","The sentence describes joining the religious profession.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","She left the priesthood to begin serving as a priest for the first time the next morning.","She entered the priesthood to begin serving as a priest the next morning.","Leaving the priesthood means leaving that role; entering it means beginning the vocation.")],quiz:[Q("priesthood.q1","priesthood.s1","meaning","The priesthood can refer to ___.",["the office or work of priests","the cost of a church building","a group of schoolchildren"],"the office or work of priests","Priesthood names the role or profession of priests.","meaning"),Q("priesthood.q2","priesthood.s1","context","If someone enters the priesthood, the person ___.",["begins a priestly religious vocation","opens a shop selling robes","leaves every religious role"],"begins a priestly religious vocation","The phrase means take up the office or work of a priest.","context"),Q("priesthood.q3","priesthood.s1","word-choice","Years of training prepared him for the ____.",["priesthood","pretense","pressure"],"priesthood","The training prepares him for the religious office and work.","word-choice"),Q("priesthood.q4","priesthood.s1","word-formation","The suffix -hood in priesthood helps form a noun for ___.",["a state, role, or condition","a person who prints books","a measurement of air"],"a state, role, or condition","-hood commonly forms nouns naming a state, role, or condition.","word-formation")]});
D("primacy",{etymology:E("From Late Latin primatia, from primas ‘of the first rank, chief’, based on Latin primus ‘first’; primacy is the state of having the leading importance or authority.",null,"primus","-acy","Etymonline, primacy (https://www.etymonline.com/word/primacy)."),contexts:[C("primacy.s1","學術","The report argues for the primacy of clean water over short-term construction goals in the river plan.","報告主張，在河川計畫中，清潔用水應優先於短期建設目標。","Primacy is the fact of being first in importance or authority.","Primacy is followed by of and the priority being asserted.","The report ranks clean water above other objectives.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The policy recognized the primacy of minor details over every major safety requirement, placing them first in importance.","The policy recognized the primacy of safety, giving it the highest importance.","Primacy means leading importance or authority; the example should identify what is given priority.")],quiz:[Q("primacy.q1","primacy.s1","meaning","The primacy of safety means safety has ___.",["the highest importance","the lowest possible cost","no influence at all"],"the highest importance","Primacy is the state of being first in importance or authority.","meaning"),Q("primacy.q2","primacy.s1","context","A constitution that gives the primacy of law means ___.",["law has the leading authority","every rule is optional","judges cannot interpret anything"],"law has the leading authority","The phrase says law takes priority over competing claims.","context"),Q("primacy.q3","primacy.s1","collocation","Complete the phrase: “the primacy ___ public health.”",["of","to","at"],"of","Primacy is commonly followed by of and the priority.","collocation"),Q("primacy.q4","primacy.s1","meaning","Which is closest to primacy?",["supremacy or first importance","a small prick","an early school"],"supremacy or first importance","Primacy concerns the leading rank or authority.","meaning")]});
D("primal",{etymology:E("From Latin primalis, from primus ‘first’; the adjective developed meanings of earliest or original, most basic, and deeply instinctive.",null,"primus","-al","Etymonline, primal (https://www.etymonline.com/word/primal)."),contexts:[C("primal.s1","歷史","Archaeologists found primal stone tools near the remains of one of the region’s earliest settlements.","考古學家在該地區最早聚落的遺址附近，發現了原始石器。","Primal can mean belonging to the earliest period of life or human history.","Primal modifies stone tools; near locates the find.","The tools come from an early stage of human society."),C("primal.s2","生活","Food, clean water, and shelter are primal needs during a natural disaster.","自然災害期間，食物、乾淨飲水和住所是最基本的需求。","Primal can mean most important or fundamental.","Primal modifies needs; during gives the situation.","These are basic necessities for survival."),C("primal.s3","心理","A sudden crash triggered a primal fear that made the child run toward her parents.","突如其來的撞擊聲引發孩子本能的恐懼，讓她跑向父母。","Primal can describe a deep instinctive feeling that is hard to control.","Primal modifies fear; that clause describes the resulting reaction.","The fear is immediate and instinctive rather than reasoned out.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","His primal response was a carefully calculated choice made after weeks of analysis, with no instinct or deep emotion involved.","His primal response was an immediate instinctive reaction to the sudden threat.","Primal in this sense describes a deep, basic instinct rather than a long, deliberate calculation.")],quiz:[Q("primal.q1","primal.s1","meaning","Primal tools are associated with ___.",["an early stage of human history","the latest digital technology","a future election"],"an early stage of human history","This sense means earliest or original.","meaning"),Q("primal.q2","primal.s2","context","Which is a primal need after a flood?",["Clean drinking water","A decorative sculpture","A second television"],"Clean drinking water","Primal can mean basic and essential for survival.","context"),Q("primal.q3","primal.s3","meaning","A primal fear is usually ___.",["deep and instinctive","a carefully rehearsed speech","a minor preference about color"],"deep and instinctive","The emotional sense refers to fundamental, instinctive reactions.","meaning"),Q("primal.q4","primal.s2","word-choice","Reliable shelter is a ____ requirement when temperatures fall below freezing.",["primal","prickly","pretentious"],"primal","Shelter becomes a basic, essential need in dangerous cold.","word-choice")]});
D("primarily",{etymology:E("From primary + -ly, forming an adverb meaning chiefly or for the most part; primary is from Latin primarius, based on primus ‘first’.",null,"primus","-ly","Etymonline, primary (https://www.etymonline.com/word/primary)."),contexts:[C("primarily.s1","通用","The fund supports primarily rural clinics, although a small share also goes to urban outreach programs.","這筆基金主要支援鄉村診所，不過也有一小部分用於都市外展計畫。","Primarily means mainly or for the most part.","Primarily modifies supports and is contrasted with the smaller share.","Most of the funding goes to rural clinics, but not all of it.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The survey was primarily about sleep, even though it asked no questions about sleep and focused entirely on diet.","The survey was primarily about diet because most of its questions concerned food and eating habits.","Primarily identifies the main focus; a survey with no sleep questions cannot mainly concern sleep.")],quiz:[Q("primarily.q1","primarily.s1","meaning","If a book is primarily about birds, it is ___.",["mainly about birds","only one page long","written before birds existed"],"mainly about birds","Primarily means mainly or for the most part.","meaning"),Q("primarily.q2","primarily.s1","context","A course uses primarily online lessons but meets in person once a month. Most lessons are ___.",["online","in person every day","not taught at all"],"online","Primarily indicates the dominant format, though exceptions exist.","context"),Q("primarily.q3","primarily.s1","word-choice","The clinic serves ____ older adults, while also accepting other patients.",["primarily","priesthood","priceless"],"primarily","Older adults are the clinic’s main group, not its only group.","word-choice"),Q("primarily.q4","primarily.s1","meaning","Does primarily mean “exclusively”?",["No; it means mainly, with possible exceptions.","Yes; it means without any exception.","No; it means at a time long ago."],"No; it means mainly, with possible exceptions.","The adverb marks the largest part or chief focus, not necessarily the whole.","meaning")]});
D("primary",{etymology:E("From Latin primarius ‘of the first rank’, from primus ‘first’; it describes what is first in importance or sequence, and the noun also names a party election or a basic color.",null,"primus","-ary","Etymonline, primary (https://www.etymonline.com/word/primary)."),contexts:[C("primary.s1","通用","Our primary goal is to keep the bridge open safely while engineers inspect its supports.","我們的首要目標是在工程師檢查橋梁支架時，確保橋梁安全開放。","Primary means most important or first in priority.","Primary modifies goal; while introduces the simultaneous inspection.","Safety is ranked above other aims during the inspection."),C("primary.s2","教育","Her son starts primary school in September after finishing the local early-learning program.","她的兒子完成當地幼兒課程後，將於九月開始上小學。","Primary can mean first in a series, especially the first years of school.","Primary modifies school and marks the early stage of education.","The child is moving from early learning into elementary education."),C("primary.s3","政治","Voters chose their party’s nominee in a primary before the general election.","選民在大選前的黨內初選中選出了政黨提名人。","A primary is an election within a political party to choose a candidate.","Primary is the object of in; before contrasts it with the later general election.","The vote selects a party’s nominee, not the officeholder directly.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","A primary goal is the least important task, chosen only after every secondary objective has been completed.","A primary goal is the most important objective and receives first attention.","Primary in the priority sense means chief or most important, not least important.")],quiz:[Q("primary.q1","primary.s1","meaning","A primary concern is ___.",["the main or most important concern","a minor detail no one values","a concern from the distant past"],"the main or most important concern","Primary ranks something first in importance.","meaning"),Q("primary.q2","primary.s2","context","A child in primary school is in ___.",["the first years of formal schooling","graduate school","a political campaign office"],"the first years of formal schooling","Primary can refer to the initial stage of schooling.","context"),Q("primary.q3","primary.s3","meaning","In US politics, a primary helps a party ___.",["select its candidate for a later election","appoint every judge directly","count votes after the election ends"],"select its candidate for a later election","A party primary chooses a nominee.","meaning"),Q("primary.q4","primary.s3","context","Which is a primary color in a basic art lesson?",["red","a mixture of red and blue","a shadow"],"red","Primary can name a basic color not made by mixing other colors.","context")]});
D("primate",{etymology:E("From Medieval Latin primatem ‘chief, high-ranking ecclesiastic’, from Late Latin primas ‘of first rank’, based on primus ‘first’; the zoological name was later applied to the order that includes humans and monkeys.",null,"primus",null,"Etymonline, primate (https://www.etymonline.com/word/primate)."),contexts:[C("primate.s1","生物","The field team watched a primate use a twig to draw insects from a narrow opening in the tree.","野外研究團隊觀察一隻靈長類動物用小枝從樹洞窄縫中取出昆蟲。","A primate is an animal in the group that includes monkeys, apes, and humans.","Primate is the object of watched; use describes the animal’s behavior.","The animal’s tool use is observed in its natural environment.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","A penguin is a primate because it lays eggs and lives near some monkeys in a zoo.","A macaque is a primate because it belongs to the mammal group that includes monkeys, apes, and humans.","Penguins are birds, whereas primates are mammals; sharing a zoo does not determine the classification.")],quiz:[Q("primate.q1","primate.s1","meaning","Which group includes primates?",["Monkeys, apes, and humans","Penguins, gulls, and owls","Salmon, trout, and eels"],"Monkeys, apes, and humans","Primate is the zoological group containing these animals.","meaning"),Q("primate.q2","primate.s1","context","A scientist studying a lemur is studying ___.",["a primate","a flowering plant","a kind of mineral"],"a primate","Lemurs belong to the order of primates.","context"),Q("primate.q3","primate.s1","word-choice","The researcher recorded how the ____ used branches as tools.",["primate","pretext","pressure"],"primate","A monkey or ape observed using tools is a primate.","word-choice"),Q("primate.q4","primate.s1","meaning","What is a primate in zoology?",["A mammal in the group including monkeys and humans","Any animal that can fly","A plant that produces fruit"],"A mammal in the group including monkeys and humans","Primate is the animal-group name, not a general label for all animals.","meaning")]});
D("primatology",{etymology:E("Coined from primate + -ology ‘study of’; primate comes from Latin primus ‘first rank’, and primatology is the zoological study of primates and their behavior and evolution.",null,"primate","-ology","Etymonline, primatology (https://www.etymonline.com/word/primate)."),contexts:[C("primatology.s1","生物","Primatology combines field observation and genetics to study how different primate groups use tools.","靈長類動物學結合野外觀察與遺傳學，研究不同靈長類群體如何使用工具。","Primatology is the branch of zoology that studies primates, their behavior, and evolution.","Primatology is the subject; to study introduces its purpose.","The field examines primates through behavioral and biological research.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","Primatology studies only ancient grammar and has no connection to monkeys, apes, or animal behavior.","Primatology studies primates such as monkeys and apes, including their behavior and evolution.","The field is defined by the scientific study of primates, not grammar.")],quiz:[Q("primatology.q1","primatology.s1","meaning","Primatology is the study of ___.",["primates and their behavior","weather systems over the ocean","ancient building materials only"],"primates and their behavior","The discipline studies primates and their biology and behavior.","meaning"),Q("primatology.q2","primatology.s1","context","Which research belongs to primatology?",["Observing how lemurs communicate and forage","Measuring rainfall on a glacier","Cataloging medieval coins"],"Observing how lemurs communicate and forage","Lemurs are primates, and their behavior is studied in this field.","context"),Q("primatology.q3","primatology.s1","word-formation","What does -ology mean in primatology?",["the study of a subject","a person who paints a wall","a measurement of pressure"],"the study of a subject","The suffix -ology forms names of fields of study.","word-formation"),Q("primatology.q4","primatology.s1","word-choice","The university launched a ____ program focused on ape evolution.",["primatology","presidency","pretense"],"primatology","Ape evolution is a topic within the study of primates.","word-choice")]});
D("prime",{etymology:E("From Old French prime and Latin primus ‘first’; the adjective means chief or excellent, the noun can mean a person’s best period or a prime number, and the verb can mean prepare beforehand.",null,"primus",null,"Etymonline, prime (https://www.etymonline.com/word/prime)."),contexts:[C("prime.s1","通用","The prime reason for delaying the launch was a faulty safety sensor.","延後發射的主要原因是安全感測器故障。","Prime can mean first or most important.","Prime modifies reason; for delaying identifies what the reason explains.","The faulty sensor is the chief cause of the delay."),C("prime.s2","通用","The singer is in her prime and can still perform the demanding role with remarkable energy.","這位歌手正值盛年，仍能以驚人的精力演出要求很高的角色。","Prime can describe the best or strongest period in someone’s life or career.","In her prime is a fixed phrase naming that peak period.","Her energy and ability indicate she is at her best."),C("prime.s3","數學","Eleven is a prime number because its only positive divisors are one and eleven.","十一是質數，因為它的正因數只有一和十一。","A prime number is an integer greater than one divisible only by one and itself.","Prime modifies number; because supplies the mathematical reason.","The divisor test shows that eleven is prime."),C("prime.s4","通用","Prime the wooden shelf with a sealing coat before applying the blue paint.","塗上藍色面漆前，先用封閉底漆處理木架。","To prime is to prepare a person, surface, or mechanism for what comes next.","Prime takes the shelf as its object; with introduces the preparatory coating.","The first coating prepares the wood for the finish paint.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The electrician chose two as a prime number because it has four positive divisors: one, two, three, and four.","The electrician chose two as a prime number because its only positive divisors are one and two.","A prime number has exactly two positive divisors, one and itself; two qualifies.")],quiz:[Q("prime.q1","prime.s1","meaning","In “the prime reason,” prime means ___.",["chief or most important","the final or least important","painted with a primer"],"chief or most important","The adjective marks the leading reason.","meaning"),Q("prime.q2","prime.s2","context","Someone in the prime of life is in ___.",["their strongest or best period","their first day at school","a room for painting"],"their strongest or best period","Prime can name the peak period of a person’s life.","context"),Q("prime.q3","prime.s3","meaning","Which number is prime?",["13","15","21"],"13","Thirteen has only two positive divisors: one and itself.","meaning"),Q("prime.q4","prime.s4","context","Why prime a wooden surface before painting?",["To prepare it for the finishing coat","To make it a prime number","To remove every layer of wood"],"To prepare it for the finishing coat","Priming applies an initial preparatory treatment to a surface.","context")]});
D("prime integer",{etymology:E("A mathematical compound of prime, from Latin primus ‘first’, and integer, from Latin integer ‘whole, untouched’; together the phrase names a whole number greater than one with exactly two positive divisors.",null,"primus + integer",null,"Etymonline, prime and integer (https://www.etymonline.com/word/prime; https://www.etymonline.com/word/integer)."),contexts:[C("prime integer.s1","數學","Thirteen is a prime integer because no whole number other than one and thirteen divides it evenly.","十三是質數，因為除了 1 和 13 之外，沒有其他整數能整除它。","A prime integer is a whole number greater than one with no positive divisors except one and itself.","Prime integer is the complement after is; because gives the divisor test.","The example satisfies the definition of a prime whole number.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","One is a prime integer because it has exactly two positive divisors, one and itself.","One is not a prime integer; a prime integer must be greater than one and have exactly two distinct positive divisors.","One has only one positive divisor, so it fails the definition of a prime integer.")],quiz:[Q("prime integer.q1","prime integer.s1","meaning","A prime integer must be ___.",["greater than one with only one and itself as positive divisors","a fraction less than zero","divisible by every whole number"],"greater than one with only one and itself as positive divisors","The definition excludes one and composite integers.","meaning"),Q("prime integer.q2","prime integer.s1","context","Why is 17 a prime integer?",["Its only positive divisors are 1 and 17.","It is divisible by 2, 3, and 5.","It is not a whole number."],"Its only positive divisors are 1 and 17.","A prime integer has no other positive factors.","context"),Q("prime integer.q3","prime integer.s1","meaning","Is 1 a prime integer?",["No; it is not greater than one and has only one positive divisor.","Yes; every integer is prime.","Yes; it has two distinct positive divisors."],"No; it is not greater than one and has only one positive divisor.","The standard definition requires an integer greater than 1 with two distinct positive divisors.","meaning"),Q("prime integer.q4","prime integer.s1","word-choice","The number 19 is a ____ because only 1 and 19 divide it evenly.",["prime integer","price list","pretension"],"prime integer","Nineteen is a whole number with exactly two positive factors.","word-choice")]});
D("prime minister",{etymology:E("From French premier ministre ‘first minister’: premier comes from Latin primarius/primus ‘first’, and ministre from Latin minister ‘servant, attendant’; the compound names a head of government.",null,"primus + minister",null,"Etymonline, prime and minister (https://www.etymonline.com/word/prime; https://www.etymonline.com/word/minister)."),contexts:[C("prime minister.s1","政治","The prime minister met the neighboring country’s leader to discuss a cross-border rail project.","總理會見鄰國領袖，討論跨境鐵路計畫。","A prime minister is the head of government in many parliamentary systems.","Prime minister is the subject; to discuss states the purpose of the meeting.","The officeholder leads the national government and conducts policy talks.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The prime minister was the ceremonial head of government in a presidential system where the president alone led the cabinet.","The president led the cabinet in that presidential system; a prime minister is the head of government in systems that use that office.","A prime minister is not simply another name for a president; the office’s role depends on the country’s system.")],quiz:[Q("prime minister.q1","prime minister.s1","meaning","A prime minister is usually ___.",["the head of government","the head librarian of a school","the owner of a railway station"],"the head of government","The office leads the government in many countries.","meaning"),Q("prime minister.q2","prime minister.s1","context","Who would normally present a government’s policy program to parliament?",["The prime minister","A price list","A primate"],"The prime minister","The prime minister leads the government and presents its program.","context"),Q("prime minister.q3","prime minister.s1","word-choice","The ____ announced the cabinet’s plan for public transport.",["prime minister","preservative","pretender"],"prime minister","The head of government announces the cabinet’s policy.","word-choice"),Q("prime minister.q4","prime minister.s1","meaning","Which phrase helps explain the historical parts of prime minister?",["first minister","whole number","paint primer"],"first minister","The title comes from French premier ministre, literally ‘first minister’.","word-formation")]});
D("primer",{etymology:E("The introductory-book sense comes from Medieval Latin primarium, from primus ‘first’, on the idea of a first book; the paint-coat sense is an agent noun from prime ‘prepare’. These histories are distinct.",null,"primus / prime","-er","Etymonline, primer (https://www.etymonline.com/word/primer)."),contexts:[C("primer.s1","教育","The beginner’s primer explains the water cycle with simple diagrams before introducing technical terms.","這本初學者入門讀本先用簡單圖表說明水循環，再介紹專業術語。","A primer is a simple introductory book for learners, or a preparatory coating applied before paint.","Primer is the subject; explains names the book’s function.","The guide introduces a topic to beginners in an accessible order."),C("primer.s1","工程","The carpenter applied a coat of primer to the bare wood so the blue finish would adhere evenly.","木匠在裸木上塗了一層底漆，讓藍色面漆能均勻附著。","A primer can also be the preparatory coat placed under paint.","Primer is the object of applied; to the bare wood states its surface.","The coat prepares the wood for a smooth layer of finishing paint.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The carpenter skipped the primer, which is the final colored coat applied after the paint has completely dried.","The carpenter applied primer first, then added the colored finishing coat after it dried.","In painting, primer is a preparatory undercoat, not the final decorative layer.")],quiz:[Q("primer.q1","primer.s1","meaning","A reading primer is ___.",["a simple introductory book for beginners","a final legal judgment","a list of prices"],"a simple introductory book for beginners","The book introduces a subject at a basic level.","meaning"),Q("primer.q2","primer.s1","context","Why apply primer before painting a wooden door?",["It prepares the surface for the finish coat.","It is the finished color layer itself.","It makes the door a prime integer."],"It prepares the surface for the finish coat.","Paint primer is a preparatory coat that helps the final paint.","context"),Q("primer.q3","primer.s1","word-choice","The course assigned a short ____ to explain basic astronomy to new students.",["primer","pressure","priesthood"],"primer","A beginner’s primer introduces the subject before advanced material.","word-choice"),Q("primer.q4","primer.s1","meaning","Why can primer mean both a first book and an undercoat?",["Both senses involve something preparatory or first in a sequence, though their word histories differ.","Both words name a type of bird.","The book sense means the paint has already peeled."],"Both senses involve something preparatory or first in a sequence, though their word histories differ.","The introductory book comes from the notion of a first book, while the paint primer is from the verb prime, to prepare.","meaning")]});
